"hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1660,"**
Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Rafi’, narrated to us Suraij ibn al-Nu’man, who said: Narrated to us Fulaikh, from Sa’eed ibn al-Harith, from Abu Salamah ibn ‘Abd al-Rahman, who said: When Abu Hurayrah passed away, I said, ""By Allah, I should go to Abu Sa’eed al-Khudri."" So I went to him and he narrated a lengthy hadith about the story of the palm branches.

Then the sky became stormy that night. When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went out for the ‘Isha prayer, a flash of lightning illuminated the sky. He (ﷺ) saw Qatadah ibn al-Nu’man and said, ""Why are you here at this hour, O Qatadah?""

Qatadah replied, ""I knew, O Messenger of Allah, that few people would attend the prayer tonight, so I wanted to attend it.""

The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""If you have prayed, then remain in your place until I pass by you.""

When he (ﷺ) finished the prayer, he (ﷺ) gave Qatadah a palm branch and said, ""Take this. It will illuminate for you ten steps ahead and ten steps behind you. When you enter your house and see darkness in a corner of the house, strike it before you speak, for it is the Shaytan.""

Qatadah did so, and we love these palm branches for that reason."
